Gamma '_{	au }\geq \Gamma _{	au }$ and $\Gamma '_{	au }\in \mathrm{PSH}(X,	heta )\cup \{ -\infty \} $ by proposition 5.14.15 for all $	au \in \mathbb {R}$. We claim that BD13D6DEBB93 17.13.13  egin{equation}  \Gamma '_{	au }\leq \Gamma _{	au }+(b-a)(\Gamma _{\max }-	au ),\quad 	au \in \mathbb {R}. \end{equation} Observe that $\Gamma '_{	au }\equiv -\infty $ when $	au >\Gamma _{\max }$ by 17.13.10 . Thus it suffices to consider $	au \leq \Gamma _{\max }$. Put \[  C_{	au }\coloneqq (b-a)(\Gamma _{\max }-	au )\geq 0.  \] For any $s\in [a,b]$, the monotonicity of $t\mapsto \Gamma _ t^*-t\Gamma _{\max }$ from 17.13.10 gives \[  \Gamma _ b^*-b	au \leq \Gamma _ s^*-s	au +C_{	au }.  \] Since $\ell _ b=\Gamma _ b^*$, we get \[  \Gamma '_{	au }\leq \Gamma _ b^*-b	au \leq \Gamma _ s^*-s	au +C_{	au },\quad s\in [a,b].  \] For $s
otin [a,b]$, we have $\ell _ s=\Gamma _ s^*$, hence \[  \Gamma '_{	au }\leq \Gamma _ s^*-s	au \leq \Gamma _ s^*-s	au +C_{	au }.  \] Taking the infimum over all $s>0$ gives \[  \Gamma '_{	au }\leq \Gamma _{	au }+C_{	au }.  \] Therefore, ( 17.13.13 ) follows. In particular, for any $	au <\Gamma _{\max }$, we have $\Gamma '_{	au }\sim \Gamma _{	au }$. Moreover, $\sup _ X\ell _ t\leq t\Gamma _{\max }$ for all $t>0$: this is clear outside $(a,b)$ from 17.13.10 , and on $(a,b)$ it follows from the convexity of subgeodesics applied to the geodesic $(\eta _ t)_{t\in (a,b)}$. Hence, for $	au <\Gamma _{\max }$, \[  \sup _ X(\ell _ t-t	au )\leq t(\Gamma _{\max }-	au ).  \] Letting $t	o 0+$ gives $\Gamma '_{	au }\leq 0$. It follows from the fact that $\Gamma _{	au }$ is a model potential that $\Gamma _{	au }=\Gamma '_{	au }$ for all $	au <\Gamma _{\max }$. Therefore, by theorem 21.11.24 , we have $\Gamma ^*_ t=\ell _ t$ for all $t>0$, which is a contradiction. $\square$ Given $\ell \in \mathcal{R}(X,	heta ;\phi )$, define its Legendre transform 10B32891AA98 17.13.14  egin{equation}  \ell ^*_{	au }\coloneqq \inf _{t>0} (\ell _ t-t	au ),\quad 	au \in \mathbb {R}. \end{equation} Lemma 17.13.15 . 7B83BD1D5FB9 Given $\ell \in \mathcal{R}(X,	heta ;\phi )$, then $\ell ^*=(\ell ^*_	au )_{	au <\sup _ X \ell _1}\in \mathrm{TC}(X,	heta ;\phi )$. Proof. Note that it follows from proposition 5.14.15 that $\ell ^*_{	au }\in \mathrm{PSH}(X,	heta )\cup \{ -\infty \} $ for all $	au \in \mathbb {R}$. It is clear that $\mathbb {R}
i 	au \mapsto \ell ^*_{	au }$ is a decreasing and concave function. By proposition 17.10.39 , \[  \sup _ X\ell _ t= t\sup _ X \ell _1 \quad  orall t\geq 0.  \] Set $C=\sup _ X\ell _1$. By proposition 17.10.39 , $\sup _ X(\ell _ t-Ct)=0$ for all $t>0$. For each $x$ outside a pluripolar set, the function $t\mapsto \ell _ t(x)-Ct$ is convex on $(0,\infty )$ and bounded above by $0$, hence it is decreasing. By proposition 5.14.6 , the same monotonicity holds as an inequality of $	heta $-psh functions. Thus $(\ell _ t-Ct)_{t>0}$ is a decreasing net in $\mathrm{PSH}(X,	heta )$. Its infimum is not identically $-\infty $, since the family is normalized by $\sup _ X(\ell _ t-Ct)=0$ and is compact in $L^1$ by proposition 5.17.3 . Therefore \[  \ell ^*_{C}=\inf _{t>0}(\ell _ t-Ct)\in \mathrm{PSH}(X,	heta )  \] by proposition 5.14.2 . On the other hand, for $	au >\sup _ X \ell _1$, the same argument shows that \[  \ell ^*_{	au }\equiv -\infty .  \] Therefore, $\ell ^*_{	au }\in \mathrm{PSH}(X,	heta )$ if and only if $	au \leq \ell ^*_{\max }\coloneqq \sup _ X \ell _1$. We claim that $(\ell ^*_{	au })_{	au <\ell ^*_{\max }}$ is a test curve. We first observe that for $	au <\ell ^*_{\max }$, we have \[  \ell ^*_{	au }\leq \ell _1-	au \sim _ P \phi .  \] Therefore, 5BF1777D23C2 17.13.16  egin{equation}  \ell ^*_{	au }\preceq _ P \phi ,\quad  orall 	au <\ell ^*_{\max }. \end{equation} Also observe that for any $	au \leq \ell ^*_{\max }$ and any $t>0$, we have \[  \sup _ X \ell ^*_{	au }\leq \sup _ X \ell _ t-t	au =\ell ^*_{\max }t-t	au .  \] Letting $t	o 0+$, we find that for any $	au \leq \ell ^*_{\max }$, we have 6F01D0840C12 17.13.17  egin{equation}  \sup _ X \ell ^*_{	au }\leq 0. \end{equation} Fix $	au <\ell ^*_{\max }$. We want to argue that 59C9610616F1 17.13.18  egin{equation}  P_{	heta }\left[\ell ^*_{	au }ight]=\ell ^*_{	au }. \end{equation} First we claim that for any $C>0$, we have 25F16D030FA9 17.13.19  egin{equation}  (\ell ^*_{	au }+C)\land \phi =(\ell ^*_{	au }+C)\